- op: discuss  # 59a7
  at: '2026-06-06T10:36:11Z'  # 59a7
  by: agent  # 59a7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 59a7
  clock: 2  # 59a7
  nonce: 59a7  # 59a7
  message: "Adds two facets on the instantiates/constructor access_mode (blind-severity-derived priority signal: P1). (1) access_mode is assigned non-deterministically per call site for the same target+construct: one class (ArityFlags) is the dst of both a 'read' instantiate (from classify_parameter_flags) and a 'write' instantiate (from compute_stable_id), for the same ast_new construct — so assignment varies per call site, not per construct. (2) Framing: instantiation (a constructor call) is not an access of the target at all, so access_mode on instantiates is semantically meaningless. instantiates edges carry access_mode write 4988 / read 678 / None 2273. Fix should make assignment per-construct deterministic (or stop assigning access_mode to instantiates)."  # 59a7
